    note for GameController "Opening is acknowledgement, not rendered combat.<br/>Midterm Continue/Retake explicitly report T10.<br/>Combat backend exists with explicit policy.<br/>Opening/Final battle presentation and endings remain pending."
    note for GameState "HP is separate from marks and energy.<br/>Returned snapshots are defensive copies.<br/>Relationships/rewards are persisted data, not playable systems yet."
    note for RuleValues "Null is TBD, never zero.<br/>No production balancing defaults.<br/>Separate opt-in Demo supplies provisional values."
    note for ContentCatalog "One Lesson node: ask OR raise hand.<br/>Fixed ordinary questions, supplied major sample size.<br/>Demo supplies four lessons and two Hub activities.<br/>Assessment banks and later content remain pending."
    note for GradeBook "65 Term / 10 Participation / 25 Final.<br/>Midterm belongs to Term; its weight is supplied explicitly.<br/>First two absences free, then minus one overall percentage point."
    note for AssessmentRecord "Ordinary including makeup: three-day delay.<br/>Midterm and Final: immediate result, no skip.<br/>Evaluator supplies mark; no HP or automatic rubric conversion."
    note for SaveManager "Only active DAY_END snapshots.<br/>Load does not advance or regrant effects.<br/>Ending/Retake autosave boundaries remain T12."
    note for JavaAssessmentRunner "Actual compiler and test processes with time/output limits.<br/>Trusted local code only, not an OS security sandbox.<br/>No automatic course-score rubric."

    note for Main "Opens the JavaFX game window only.<br/>Arguments are ignored: no CLI routes, modes or day jumps.<br/>FXGL and libGDX are prepared by Gradle, not started."
    note for GameSession "Frontend controller: never edits GameState.<br/>Refusals become Pending/Rejected with nothing changed.<br/>showLesson() is called once per class."
    note for CombatEvaluations "One evaluation at a time; results return on the UI thread.<br/>Leaving the combat drops late results.<br/>A failed or refused result keeps the ticket and work for a retry."
    note for CombatScreen "Displays the backend view only: no UI timing, weights, HP or marks.<br/>No pause while a question's clock runs.<br/>No evaluator shipped: submission reports T06 (Lab) or T07."
    note for LabRunService "One run at a time; results return on the UI thread.<br/>Edits make older results stale.<br/>Evidence-to-mark is T06; Lab problems not supplied yet."

    GameController --> CombatRules : explicit decisions
    GameState *-- CombatSession : copied transient assessment state
    CombatSession --> Question : difficulty-ranked content
    note for CombatRules "30s soft threshold and Combo +5 are confirmed.<br/>HP formula, score conversion and ambiguous composition require explicit policy."
    note for CombatSession "Backend monotonic clock and stale-result tickets.<br/>Final completed answer gets Dasher.<br/>Reward delays are not inventory/effect operations.<br/>No mid-combat save."
